2. Iska "Binary Search" se kya lena-dena hai? 🤔
Normal Binary Search mein hum kya karte hain? Ek sorted array mein mid nikaalte hain aur check karte hain ki target left mein hai ya right mein.
Binary Search on Answer mein hum "Answer" par binary search chalate hain. Humari range kya hai? low = 1 ghanta aur high = 6 ghante.

Step 1: Humne mid nikala: (1 + 6) / 2 = 3 ghante.
Step 2: Humne papa se pucha, "Papa kya 3 ghante padhne par console milega?" (Ye humara check function hai). Papa ne bola, "Nahi! (False)".
Step 3: Sabse important decision!

Kyunki 3 ghante par answer False aaya hai, toh kya 1 ya 2 ghante padhne par console mil sakta hai? Kabhi nahi!
Yani hume pakka pata chal gaya ki answer left side (1 se 3 ke beech) nahi ho sakta.
Hume left side ko check karne ki zaroorat hi nahi hai! Hum seedhe apni search space ko right mein shift kar denge: low = mid + 1 (yani 4).

Step 4: Nayi search space hai [4, 5, 6]. mid nikala: (4 + 6) / 2 = 5 ghante.
Step 5: Check kiya: Kya 5 ghante par console milega? Papa ne bola, "Haan! (True)".
Step 6: Agla decision!

Kyunki 5 ghante par True hai, toh ho sakta hai isse kam padhne par bhi console mil jaye (jaise 4 ghante par). Lekin 6 ghante check karne ka koi fayda nahi hai kyunki woh toh True hoga hi
Hume sabse minimum ghante dhundhne hain jahan se True shuru ho rha hai
Isliye hum right side ko chhod denge aur left mein check karenge: high = mid - 1 (yani 4) aur 5 ko temporary answer mein save kar lenge.

******************************************************************************************************

📌 Summary (Dimaag mein fit karne ke liye)
> Normal Binary Search: Hum kisi value ko array ke andar dhoondhte hain.

> Binary Search on Answer: Hum direct answer ko guess karte hain (range low se high ke beech) aur
    phir ek function banakar check karte hain ki kya ye answer valid hai.

> Monotonicity: Agar answer valid hai, toh uske aage ke saare answers bhi valid honge.
    Is property ki wajah se hum bina sabko check kiye, aadhi range ko ek baar mein reject kar sakte hain.